(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["test11_2A"] = [{"id":"dcd9ad50","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is adapted from George Eliot’s 1857 short story “The Sad Fortunes of the Rev. Amos Barton.” Mr. Ely is a clergyman in the town of Milby. By the laity of Milby and its neighbourhood [Mr. Ely] was regarded as a man of quite remarkable powers and learning, who must make a considerable sensation in London pulpits and drawing-rooms on his occasional visit to the metropolis; and by his brother clergy he was regarded as a discreet and agreeable fellow. Mr. Ely never got into a warm discussion; he suggested what might be thought, but rarely said what he thought himself; he never let either men or women see that he was laughing at them, and he never gave any one an opportunity of laughing at him.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from George Eliot’s 1857 short story “The Sad Fortunes of the Rev. Amos Barton.” Mr. Ely is a clergyman in the town","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of Milby.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"By the laity of Milby and its neighbourhood [Mr. Ely] was regarded as a man of quite remarkable powers and learning, who must","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"make a considerable sensation in London pulpits and drawing-rooms on his occasional visit to the metropolis; and by his brother","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"clergy he was regarded as a discreet and agreeable fellow. Mr. Ely never got into a warm discussion; he suggested what might be","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"thought, but rarely said what he thought himself; he never let either men or women see that he was laughing at them, and he never","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"gave any one an opportunity of laughing at him.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It shows that Mr. Ely had originally been held in high regard by his friends and then details the events that caused their regard for him to subside.","It implies that Mr. Ely’s neighbors are more naïve in their estimation of him than people in London are and then explains why his neighbors have been so easily misled.","It stresses the discrepancy between Mr. Ely’s public and private conduct and then alludes to his motivation for hiding his true personality.","It presents the favorable opinion of Mr. Ely that other people hold and then describes the behaviors of Mr. Ely that enable him to maintain that favorable opinion."]},{"id":"6ae393f7","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Asteroid 6478 Gault has experienced intermittent mass loss since at least 2013, but in contrast to some other asteroids with repeated mass-loss episodes, 6478 Gault has not lost mass at its perihelion (the closest point of its orbit to the Sun), and thus the loss is not attributable to solar energy – driven ice vaporization. And as Jane X. Luu et al. point out, the singular nature of impact ejection makes it untenable as an account of multiple loss episodes of similar duration over several years. Instead, Luu et al. are likely correct that 6478 Gault is shedding mass due to rotational instability.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Asteroid 6478 Gault has experienced intermittent mass loss since at least 2013, but in contrast to some other asteroids with repeated mass-loss","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"episodes, 6478 Gault has not lost mass at its perihelion (the closest point of its orbit to the Sun), and thus the loss is not attributable to solar","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"energy–driven ice vaporization. And as Jane X. Luu et al. point out, the singular nature of impact ejection makes it untenable as an account of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"multiple loss episodes of similar duration over several years. Instead, Luu et al. are likely correct that 6478 Gault is shedding mass due to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"rotational instability.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It presents a scientific observation, describes a contrast between that observation and other observations, and then explains why those other observations should not be considered credible.","It describes an astronomical finding, discusses competing theories about that finding that the author regards as flawed, and then describes new evidence that supports an alternative theory.","It introduces a natural phenomenon, refutes two potential explanations for that phenomenon, and then presents a third explanation for that phenomenon that the author regards as plausible.","It discusses a physical process, evaluates possible causes of that process, and then states that a persuasive account of the process has yet to be put forward."]},{"id":"1107e7dc","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Economists often assert that countries looking to increase their reliance on solar energy should expand their capacity for storage; having an ample reserve of stored energy can mitigate the effects of ______ solar energy collection caused by unpredictable shifts in cloud cover and haze.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Economists often assert that countries looking to increase their reliance on solar energy should expand their capacity for storage; having an","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"ample reserve of stored energy can mitigate the effects of ______ solar energy collection caused by unpredictable shifts in cloud cover and haze.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["developments of","fluctuations in","calibrations with","incentives for"]},{"id":"cf9a00e0","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Chile’s Atacama Desert is one of the driest places on Earth. Mary Beth Wilhelm and other astrobiologists search for life, or its remains, in this harsh place because the desert closely mirrors the extreme environment on Mars. The algae and bacteria found in Atacama’s driest regions may offer clues about Martian life. By studying how these and other microorganisms survive such extreme conditions on Earth, Wilhelm’s team hopes to determine whether similar life might have existed on Mars and to develop the best tools to look for evidence of it.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Chile’s Atacama Desert is one of the driest places on Earth. Mary Beth Wilhelm and other astrobiologists search for life, or its remains, in this","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"harsh place because the desert closely mirrors the extreme environment on Mars. The algae and bacteria found in Atacama’s driest regions may","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"offer clues about Martian life. By studying how these and other microorganisms survive such extreme conditions on Earth, Wilhelm’s team hopes","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"to determine whether similar life might have existed on Mars and to develop the best tools to look for evidence of it.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["To contrast the conditions in the Atacama Desert with those on Mars","To explain why many life-forms cannot survive in the Atacama Desert","To indicate why astrobiologists choose to conduct research in the Atacama Desert","To describe certain limitations to conducting scientific study in the Atacama Desert"],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Mary Beth Wilhelm and other astrobiologists search for life, or its remains, in this","harsh place because the desert closely mirrors the extreme environment on Mars."]},{"id":"dc234d74","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The recently observed gamma ray burst GRB 230307A lasted for 200 seconds, ______ for a burst generated by the merger of neutron stars. Bursts caused by neutron mergers typically last fewer than 2 seconds.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The recently observed gamma ray burst GRB 230307A lasted for 200 seconds, ______ for a burst generated by the merger of neutron stars.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Bursts caused by neutron mergers typically last fewer than 2 seconds.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["a coincidence","a reprieve","an incident","an oddity"]},{"id":"edbc6cca","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Bram Stoker’s 1911 novel The Lair of the White Worm. Adam is meeting his great-uncle Richard at a port. The meeting so auspiciously begun proceeded well. Adam, seeing that the old man was interested in the novelty of the ship, suggested that he should stay the night on board, and that he would himself be ready to start at any hour and go anywhere that the other suggested. This affectionate willingness to fall in with his own plans quite won the old man’s heart. He warmly accepted the invitation, and at once they became not only on terms of affectionate relationship, but almost like old friends.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Bram Stoker’s 1911 novel The Lair of the White Worm. Adam is meeting his great-uncle Richard at a port.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"The meeting so auspiciously begun proceeded well. Adam, seeing that the old man was interested in the novelty of the ship,","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"suggested that he should stay the night on board, and that he would himself be ready to start at any hour and go anywhere that","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"the other suggested. This affectionate willingness to fall in with his own plans quite won the old man’s heart. He warmly accepted","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"the invitation, and at once they became not only on terms of affectionate relationship, but almost like old friends.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["It states the reasons why Adam and his great-uncle Richard decide to sleep on the ship rather than finding lodging on land.","It showcases how Adam’s flexibility and consideration strengthen his relationship with his great-uncle Richard.","It describes why Adam and his great-uncle Richard are excited for their upcoming journey on the ship.","It contrasts great-uncle Richard’s wary first impressions of Adam with his ultimate affection toward him."]},{"id":"d5600e74","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is adapted from Pam Mu ñoz Ryan’s 2020 novel Mañanaland. In the village where Max lives, there is an old fortress called La Reina. Children in the village say that the fortress is haunted. For as long as he could remember, Max had begged Pap á [his father] to take him to see La Reina and the ruins up close. He d be a hero among his friends if he was the first boy to cross the haunted gates! Just because Pap á didn’t believe in ghosts didn’t mean they weren’t there. Maybe this summer Pap á would finally take him. He was almost twelve. ©2020 by Pam Mu ñoz Ryan","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from Pam Muñoz Ryan’s 2020 novel Mañanaland. In the village where Max lives, there is an old fortress called La","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Reina. Children in the village say that the fortress is haunted.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"For as long as he could remember, Max had begged Papá [his father] to take him to see La Reina and the ruins up close. He’d be a","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"hero among his friends if he was the first boy to cross the haunted gates! Just because Papá didn’t believe in ghosts didn’t mean","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"they weren’t there. Maybe this summer Papá would finally take him. He was almost twelve.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"©2020 by Pam Muñoz Ryan","indent":4}],"question":"Which choice best describes the overall purpose of the text?","choices":["To portray how proud Max’s father is of Max","To explain why Max doesn’t want to grow up yet","To criticize Max for disliking summer","To show how much Max wants to visit La Reina"]},{"id":"2390e956","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Ronyoung Kim creatively captures the Korean American immigrant experience in her novel Clay Walls by writing about a family from three ______ perspectives. The first section of the novel is from the mother Haesu’s perspective, the second is from the father Chun’s perspective, and the last is from the daughter Faye’s perspective.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Ronyoung Kim creatively captures the Korean American immigrant experience in her novel Clay Walls by writing about a family from three ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"perspectives. The first section of the novel is from the mother Haesu’s perspective, the second is from the father Chun’s perspective, and the last","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"is from the daughter Faye’s perspective.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?","choices":["distinct","required","unintended","unknown"]},{"id":"3cc7d73b","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Using the Stratospheric Observatory for Infrared Astronomy (SOFIA), a team of astronomers mapped out the magnetic field of G47, one of the Milky Way’s galactic bones (dense clouds of gas and dust that run through the middle of the arm of a spiral galaxy). Surprisingly, the map revealed a magnetic field with no clear pattern or direction. The researchers had expected the magnetic field to be similar to the more uniform fields seen in galactic bones in other arms of the Milky Way.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Using the Stratospheric Observatory for Infrared Astronomy (SOFIA), a team of astronomers mapped out the magnetic field of G47, one of the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Milky Way’s galactic bones (dense clouds of gas and dust that run through the middle of the arm of a spiral galaxy). Surprisingly, the map","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"revealed a magnetic field with no clear pattern or direction. The researchers had expected the magnetic field to be similar to the more uniform","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"fields seen in galactic bones in other arms of the Milky Way.","indent":0}],"question":"According to the text, what was surprising about the researchers’ mapping of the magnetic field of galactic bone G47?","choices":["It showed a weaker magnetic field than expected.","It implied that previous mappings of the magnetic field were inaccurate.","It produced magnetic field measurements similar to those for other galactic bones.","It revealed a magnetic field that wasn’t uniform."]},{"id":"c088a9a9","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Over the course of the 1900s, more and more Native Hawaiians spoke English instead of the Hawaiian language. To preserve their language, Native Hawaiian teachers founded the Aha P ‘ ūnana Leo preschool in 1984. They spoke Hawaiian while teaching, and their Native Hawaiian students were soon able to understand and speak it themselves. The school was a huge success. Eventually it opened locations around Hawai i ‘ and started teaching Hawaiian to elementary and high school students too. Thanks to Aha P ‘ ūnana Leo, the number of young people who speak the language has increased.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Over the course of the 1900s, more and more Native Hawaiians spoke English instead of the Hawaiian language. To preserve their language,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Native Hawaiian teachers founded the ‘Aha Pūnana Leo preschool in 1984. They spoke Hawaiian while teaching, and their Native Hawaiian","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"students were soon able to understand and speak it themselves. The school was a huge success. Eventually it opened locations around Hawai‘i","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"and started teaching Hawaiian to elementary and high school students too. Thanks to ‘Aha Pūnana Leo, the number of young people who speak","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the language has increased.","indent":0}],"question":"Which statement, if true, would most directly support the underlined claim?","choices":["Fewer than fifty children could speak Hawaiian when Aha P ūnana Leo was founded, but now more than 2,000 students at ‘Aha Pūnana Leo speak it.","Roughly 680,000 Native Hawaiian people lived in the United States in 2020, and a little less than half of them lived in Hawai i. ‘","Hawaiian is very similar to other languages that are spoken on the Polynesian Islands of the Pacific Ocean, including Tahitian, Samoan, and M āori. ‘","Besides Native Hawaiians, tens of thousands of people from other Pacific Islander communities live in Hawai i today, including over 37,000 Samoans."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Thanks to ‘Aha Pūnana Leo, the number of young people who speak","the language has increased."]},{"id":"e1504a2a","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"The Cretaceous pterosaur Tupandactylus navigans is known for having an anomalously oversized head crest. Until an almost complete fossil skeleton was found in Brazil, paleontologists had been able to study only skull specimens from T. navigans, though it was presumed that, like other pterosaurs, the species’s primary form of locomotion was powered flight. Examining the fuller skeleton in 2016, Victor Beccari and his team determined that T. navigans had long hind legs, short wings, and an unusually long neck — characteristics that, combined with the creature’s large-crested head, would have made sustained flight difficult and walking upright relatively comfortable. Based on these findings the team suggests that T. navigans likely ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The Cretaceous pterosaur Tupandactylus navigans is known for having an anomalously oversized head crest. Until an almost complete fossil","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"skeleton was found in Brazil, paleontologists had been able to study only skull specimens from T. navigans, though it was presumed that, like","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"other pterosaurs, the species’s primary form of locomotion was powered flight. Examining the fuller skeleton in 2016, Victor Beccari and his","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"team determined that T. navigans had long hind legs, short wings, and an unusually long neck—characteristics that, combined with the creature’s","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"large-crested head, would have made sustained flight difficult and walking upright relatively comfortable. Based on these findings the team","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"suggests that T. navigans likely ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["flew for longer distances than did other pterosaur species that had oversized head crests.","had longer wings than other pterosaur species considered to have been comfortable walking.","had a smaller head than researchers expected based on the earlier T. navigans skull specimens.","flew for shorter distances and spent more time walking than researchers previously thought."]},{"id":"5b74feb9","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Political scientists who favor the traditional view of voter behavior claim that voting in an election does not change a voter’s attitude toward the candidates in that election. Focusing on each US presidential election from 1976 to 1996, Ebonya Washington and Sendhil Mullainathan tested this claim by distinguishing between subjects who had just become old enough to vote (around half of whom actually voted) and otherwise similar subjects who were slightly too young to vote (and thus none of whom voted). Washington and Mullainathan compared the attitudes of the groups of subjects toward the winning candidate two years after each election.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Political scientists who favor the traditional view of voter behavior claim that voting in an election does not change a voter’s attitude toward the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"candidates in that election. Focusing on each US presidential election from 1976 to 1996, Ebonya Washington and Sendhil Mullainathan tested","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"this claim by distinguishing between subjects who had just become old enough to vote (around half of whom actually voted) and otherwise","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"similar subjects who were slightly too young to vote (and thus none of whom voted). Washington and Mullainathan compared the attitudes of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the groups of subjects toward the winning candidate two years after each election.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding from Washington and Mullainathan’s study, if true, would most directly weaken the claim made by people who favor the traditional view of voter behavior?","choices":["Subjects’ attitudes toward the winning candidate two years after a given election were strongly predicted by subjects’ general political orientation, regardless of whether subjects were old enough to vote at the time of the election.","Subjects who were not old enough to vote in a given election held significantly more positive attitudes towards the winning candidate two years later than they held at the time of the election.","Subjects who voted in a given election held significantly more polarized attitudes toward the winning candidate two years later than did subjects who were not old enough to vote in that election.","Two years after a given election, subjects who voted and subjects who were not old enough to vote were significantly more likely to express negative attitudes than positive attitudes toward the winning candidate in that election."]},{"id":"e2829dd7","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Number of Infrared Beam Breaks by Mice Treated with CNO or Saline, by Sex 1,500 Number of beam breaks 1,000 500 0 -4 10 24 38 52 66 80 94 108 122 136 150 Minutes from treatment females with saline males with saline males with CNO females with CNO To investigate the influence of certain estrogen-responsive neurons on energy expenditure, biologist Stephanie Correa et al. treated female and male mice with either saline solution or clozapine-N4-oxide (CNO), which activates the neurons. Monitoring the activity levels of the mice by measuring how frequently the animals broke infrared beams crossing their enclosures, Correa et al. found that the mice in their study showed sex-specific differences in response to neuron activation: ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Number of Infrared Beam Breaks by Mice Treated with CNO or Saline, by Sex — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"To investigate the influence of certain estrogen-responsive neurons on energy expenditure, biologist Stephanie Correa et al. treated female and male mice with either saline solution or clozapine-N4-oxide (CNO), which activates the neurons. Monitoring the activity levels of the mice by measuring how frequently the animals broke infrared beams crossing their enclosures, Correa et al. found that the mice in their study showed sex-specific differences in response to neuron activation: ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the assertion?","choices":["the four groups of mice differed greatly in their activity levels before treatment but showed identical activity levels at the end of the monitoring period.","saline-treated females showed substantially more activity at certain points in the monitoring period than saline-treated males did.","CNO-treated females showed more activity relative to saline-treated females than CNO-treated males showed relative to saline-treated males.","CNO-treated males showed a substantial decline in activity during the monitoring period, followed by a steep increase in activity at the end."]},{"id":"d047abca","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"Narwhals are shy whales that live in the remote Arctic Ocean. Some of them have a long tusk, like a unicorn horn, with sensitive nerves. Narwhals are known for this tusk, but many actually don’t have one and its purpose is unknown. One group of scientists came up with a possible purpose in 2014. The scientists suggested that the tusk may help narwhals determine when water around them is likely to start freezing and become dangerous for them. Marine biologist Kristin Laidre disagrees with that idea, though. She reasons that if the narwhal’s tusk serves such an important purpose, then it’s most likely that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Narwhals are shy whales that live in the remote Arctic Ocean. Some of them have a long tusk, like a unicorn horn, with sensitive nerves. Narwhals","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"are known for this tusk, but many actually don’t have one and its purpose is unknown. One group of scientists came up with a possible purpose","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"in 2014. The scientists suggested that the tusk may help narwhals determine when water around them is likely to start freezing and become","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"dangerous for them. Marine biologist Kristin Laidre disagrees with that idea, though. She reasons that if the narwhal’s tusk serves such an","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"important purpose, then it’s most likely that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["some narwhals would seek a new habitat.","fewer marine animals would also have tusks.","more narwhals would have a tusk.","narwhals would become less shy over time."]},{"id":"3d505895","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"Parthenogenesis is a form of reproduction in which a female reproduces without mating. She produces an egg containing a single offspring whose DNA, or genetic material, comes entirely from its mother. Among birds, parthenogenesis has been found in a handful of species, including pigeons and turkeys. When scientists at the San Diego Zoo analyzed the DNA of the zoo’s California condors (a species of vulture), they discovered that two individuals weren’t genetically similar enough to any of the males in the condor enclosure to be their offspring. However, both had hatched from eggs laid by females in the enclosure. Thus, the scientists concluded that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Parthenogenesis is a form of reproduction in which a female reproduces without mating. She produces an egg containing a single offspring","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"whose DNA, or genetic material, comes entirely from its mother. Among birds, parthenogenesis has been found in a handful of species, including","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"pigeons and turkeys. When scientists at the San Diego Zoo analyzed the DNA of the zoo’s California condors (a species of vulture), they","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"discovered that two individuals weren’t genetically similar enough to any of the males in the condor enclosure to be their offspring. However,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"both had hatched from eggs laid by females in the enclosure. Thus, the scientists concluded that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["at least one of those individuals’ mothers was born as a result of parthenogenesis.","California condors may reproduce through parthenogenesis in zoos but not in the wild.","the mothers of the two individuals probably reproduced through parthenogenesis.","California condors reproduce through parthenogenesis only if females lack sufficient access to males."]},{"id":"fa07bcb6","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Ganga is a folk singing tradition that originated in the Dinaric Alps in southern Europe. Ganga singers sing different melodies at the same time. The clashing notes can echo a long way across the mountains, which is why ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Ganga is a folk singing tradition that originated in the Dinaric Alps in southern Europe. Ganga singers sing different melodies at the same time.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"The clashing notes can echo a long way across the mountains, which is why ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["ganga has been used as a communication method?","ganga has been used as a communication method.","has ganga been used as a communication method.","has ganga been used as a communication method?"]},{"id":"4565a53c","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Lucía Michel of the University of Chile observed that alkaline soils contain an insoluble form of iron that blueberry plants cannot absorb, thus inhibiting blueberry growth. If these plants were grown in alkaline soil alongside grasses that aid in iron solubilization, ______ Michel was determined to find out.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Lucía Michel of the University of Chile observed that alkaline soils contain an insoluble form of iron that blueberry plants cannot absorb, thus","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"inhibiting blueberry growth. If these plants were grown in alkaline soil alongside grasses that aid in iron solubilization, ______ Michel was","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"determined to find out.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["could the blueberries thrive.","the blueberries could thrive.","the blueberries could thrive?","could the blueberries thrive?"]},{"id":"6997261f","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"In 2009, researchers determined that pottery fragments from a cave in China were close to 18,000 years old. These are some of the oldest ______ of pottery ever found.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 2009, researchers determined that pottery fragments from a cave in China were close to 18,000 years old. These are some of the oldest ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of pottery ever found.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["pieces:","pieces,","pieces","pieces —"]},{"id":"3580533b","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"In recent years, economists around the world have created new tools that quantify the overall well-being of a country’s citizens. Economists in India, for example, use an Ease of Living Index. This tool ______ economic potential, sustainability, and citizens’ quality of life.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In recent years, economists around the world have created new tools that quantify the overall well-being of a country’s citizens. Economists in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"India, for example, use an Ease of Living Index. This tool ______ economic potential, sustainability, and citizens’ quality of life.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["measures","had measured","would have measured","will have been measuring"]},{"id":"7a0d9031","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"In many of her landscape paintings from the 1970s and 1980s, Lebanese American artist Etel Adnan worked to capture the essence of California’s fog-shrouded Mount Tamalpais region through abstraction, using splotches of color to represent the area’s features. Interestingly, the triangle representing the mountain itself ______ among the few defined figures in her paintings.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In many of her landscape paintings from the 1970s and 1980s, Lebanese American artist Etel Adnan worked to capture the essence of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"California’s fog-shrouded Mount Tamalpais region through abstraction, using splotches of color to represent the area’s features. Interestingly, the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"triangle representing the mountain itself ______ among the few defined figures in her paintings.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["are","have been","were","is"]},{"id":"e92a7ad3","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"In the Inca Empire (1438 – 1533), ayllus ______ family clans that ranged in size from small groups to thousands of people.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["is","was","has been","were"]},{"id":"d10e46a2","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"The ancient Spartans were known for their bitingly concise — or laconic— wit, a quality they maintained even in the face of great peril. ______ when Philip II of Macedon threatened Laconia (the region of Greece containing Sparta), he said, “If I invade Laconia, I shall turn you out.” The Spartans replied with a single word: If.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The ancient Spartans were known for their bitingly concise—or laconic—wit, a quality they maintained even in the face of great peril. ______ when","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Philip II of Macedon threatened Laconia (the region of Greece containing Sparta), he said, “If I invade Laconia, I shall turn you out.” The Spartans","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"replied with a single word: “If.”","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Rather,","In other words,","That said,","For instance,"]},{"id":"3b02e88a","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: The ancient Arab dhow was a sailing vessel distinguishable by its triangular sails and stitched hull construction. Dhows were used primarily for trade along the coasts of Arab, South Asian, and East African countries. Contemporary shipbuilders in Oman use a mix of modern and traditional materials to build replicas of ancient dhows. Most of the materials used are traditional. Replica hulls are stitched together using the same traditional coconut palm fiber rope used on the hulls of ancient dhows. The student wants to make a generalization about the materials used in dhow replicas.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"The ancient Arab dhow was a sailing vessel distinguishable by its triangular sails and stitched hull construction.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Dhows were used primarily for trade along the coasts of Arab, South Asian, and East African countries.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Contemporary shipbuilders in Oman use a mix of modern and traditional materials to build replicas of ancient dhows.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Most of the materials used are traditional.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Replica hulls are stitched together using the same traditional coconut palm fiber rope used on the hulls of ancient dhows.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["A traditional material that was used to stitch together the hulls of ancient dhows, coconut palm fiber rope is still used by shipbuilders.","The ancient Arab dhow was a sailing vessel used primarily for trade and distinguishable by its triangular sails.","Although most materials used in dhow replicas are traditional, some modern materials are used.","Contemporary shipbuilders in Oman build replicas of the dhow, which was an ancient sailing vessel with a stitched hull construction."]},{"id":"a266d876","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Upper-atmospheric jets — phenomena whereby electrical discharges cause narrow cones of blue light to briefly burst upward from the tops of thunderclouds —have been observed reaching the ionosphere. The extreme altitudes involved (the ionosphere begins about 80 km above Earth) mark these gigantic jets as outliers; ______ the majority of jets reach heights of only 20 to 50 km.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Upper-atmospheric jets—phenomena whereby electrical discharges cause narrow cones of blue light to briefly burst upward from the tops of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"thunderclouds—have been observed reaching the ionosphere. The extreme altitudes involved (the ionosphere begins about 80 km above Earth)","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"mark these gigantic jets as outliers; ______ the majority of jets reach heights of only 20 to 50 km.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["nevertheless,","consequently,","indeed,","in addition,"]},{"id":"804928b6","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Mary Kang is a Korean American portrait photographer. She is based in New York City and in Austin, Texas. One of Kang’s photographs features artist Dominique Fung. In the portrait, Fung is seated on the floor. Five of Fung’s paintings are resting against the wall behind her. The student wants to describe where Fung is in the photograph to an audience already familiar with Kang and Fung.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Mary Kang is a Korean American portrait photographer.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"She is based in New York City and in Austin, Texas.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"One of Kang’s photographs features artist Dominique Fung.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"In the portrait, Fung is seated on the floor.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Five of Fung’s paintings are resting against the wall behind her.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Dominique Fung is in a photograph by Mary Kang, a portrait photographer based in New York City and Austin, Texas.","Mary Kang is a photographer based in both New York City and Austin, Texas.","Five paintings by artist Dominique Fung can be seen in the background of Mary Kang’s photograph.","In Kang’s portrait of her, Fung is seated on the floor, with five of her paintings resting against the wall behind her."]},{"id":"a7a944ed","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In astrophysics, a ring of debris orbiting a larger object within the object’s Roche limit is expected to persist as a ring, whereas a ring of debris orbiting outside this limit would likely accrete into a satellite (e.g., a moon). Bruno Morgado and colleagues, ______ detected a dense ring of material orbiting the trans-Neptunian object Quaoar at a distance of 2,500 miles, well outside the calculated Roche limit of 1,100 miles, that has remained intact.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In astrophysics, a ring of debris orbiting a larger object within the object’s Roche limit is expected to persist as a ring, whereas a ring of debris","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"orbiting outside this limit would likely accrete into a satellite (e.g., a moon). Bruno Morgado and colleagues, ______ detected a dense ring of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"material orbiting the trans-Neptunian object Quaoar at a distance of 2,500 miles, well outside the calculated Roche limit of 1,100 miles, that has","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"remained intact.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["though,","for example,","fittingly,","likewise,"]},{"id":"dd11e5ab","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Muckrakers were journalists who sought to expose corruption in US institutions during the Progressive Era (1897 –1920). Ida Tarbell was a muckraker who investigated the Standard Oil Company. She interviewed Standard Oil Company executives, oil industry workers, and public officials. She examined thousands of pages of the company’s internal communications, including letters and financial records. Her book The History of the Standard Oil Company (1904) exposed the company’s unfair business practices. The student wants to emphasize the thoroughness of Ida Tarbell’s investigation of the Standard Oil Company.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Muckrakers were journalists who sought to expose corruption in US institutions during the Progressive Era (1897–1920).","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Ida Tarbell was a muckraker who investigated the Standard Oil Company.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"She interviewed Standard Oil Company executives, oil industry workers, and public officials.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"She examined thousands of pages of the company’s internal communications, including letters and financial records.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Her book The History of the Standard Oil Company (1904) exposed the company’s unfair business practices.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ida Tarbell not only interviewed Standard Oil executives, oil industry workers, and public officials but also examined thousands of pages of the company’s internal communications.","Ida Tarbell, who investigated the Standard Oil Company, was a muckraker (a journalist who sought to expose corruption in US institutions during the Progressive Era, 1897 – 1920).","As part of her investigation of the Standard Oil Company, muckraker Ida Tarbell conducted interviews.","Published in 1904, muckraker Ida Tarbell’s book The History of the Standard Oil Company exposed the company’s unfair business practices."]}];
